# This directory is created by git on demand.
#
# `public/uploads/projects/` is where images published through the admin end up.
# It is empty in a fresh clone because the directory itself is not tracked by
# git — only files are. This file exists so the path survives a clone, which
# means the owner can drop an image in by hand, and so the structure is visible
# in the repository rather than appearing only after the first upload.
#
# Nothing reads this directory at build time; the admin writes through the
# GitHub API, which creates the path on the first commit. The placeholder is
# convenience, not a requirement.
